  "notes": "Warren J. Smith, Modern Lens Design, 2nd ed., Figure 16.16, p. 291. Book: EFL 100, BFL 8.073, NA -0.3374 (F/1.48), GIH 5.59 (HFOV=3.20), PTZ/F 46.1, VL 88.58, infinite conjugate. The book does not mark the stop; it is placed at surface 1, the front element. The table gives thicknesses without sign; spaces after an odd number of reflections are entered negative, which reproduces the book's VL. The table lists a Mangin mirror as entry surface, reflecting back surface and exit surface (the same physical surface twice); the reflecting surface is the one the light returns from. The secondary mirror is the rear surface of the second element (surfaces 4 and 8). Central obscuration and baffles are not modelled.",
